  pages    = "963--970",
  abstract = "Embryonic stem cells (ESCs) posses the ability to self-renew and
              differentiate into a multitude of lineages, including the
              osteogenic lineage in vitro. Currently, most approaches have
              focused on embryonic body (EB)-mediated osteogenic
              differentiation, which relies on formation of all three germ
