  journal  = "Stem Cells Dev.",
  abstract = "Abstract Osteogenic differentiation of human mesenchymal stem
              cells (hMSCs) is classically thought to be mediated by different
              cytokines such as the bone morphogenetic proteins (BMPs). Here, we
              report that cell adhesion to extracellular matrix (ECM), and its
              effects on cell shape and cytoskeletal mechanics, regulates
              BMP-induced signaling and osteogenic differentiation of hMSCs.
              Using micropatterned substrates to progressively restrict cell
