  volume   =  14,
  number   =  6,
  pages    = "632--642",
  abstract = "Therapeutic modalities aimed at bone regeneration are increasingly
              employing extracellular matrix (ECM) constituents to control bone
              marrow progenitor cell (BMPC) commitment, growth, and
              differentiation. However, the precise role these ECM elements play
              during stem cell differentiation remains unclear. (See also
              Salaszynk et al., Stem Cells Dev 14(6):608-620, 2005; and Schwartz
