  journal  = "Calcif. Tissue Int.",
  volume   =  72,
  number   =  5,
  pages    = "537--547",
  abstract = "Numerous techniques are currently used to characterize biological
              mineralization in intact tissues and cell cultures; the von Kossa
              staining method, electron microscopic analysis (EM), X-ray
              diffraction, and Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR)
              are among the most common. In this study, we utilized three of
              these methods to compare the mineralization of cultured fetal rat
              calvarial cells (FRC) and the osteoblast cell lines 2T3 and
              MC3T3-E1 with the in vivo mineral of rat calvarial bone. The cells
