              increased in SUM1315 and MDA-MB-231BO cells in a β1
              -integrin-dependent manner after growing for 3 days on hOBM
              compared with tissue culture plastic. In conclusion, our results
              show that extracellular matrices derived from human osteoblasts
              represent a powerful experimental platform to dissect mechanisms
              underlying critical steps in the development of bone metastases.
