              tissue scaffolds that are integral to many regenerative therapies.
              The methodology presented provides online quantitative evaluation
              of the complex process of scaffold formation in supercritical
              environments. The capabilities of the developed system are
              demonstrated through comparison of scaffolds formed from polymers
              with different molecular weight and with different venting times.
              Visual monitoring of scaffold fabrication enabled key events in
              the supercritical processing of the scaffolds to be identified
              including the onset of polymer plasticization, supercritical
              points and foam formation. Image processing of images acquired
              during the foaming process enabled quantitative tracking of the
              growing scaffold boundary that provided new insight into the
