  pages    = "9467--9476",
  abstract = "Matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry
              imaging is an emerging powerful technique in drug metabolism and
              pharmacokinetics research. Despite recent progress in
              mass-spectrometry-based localization and relative quantification
              of small-molecule drugs and their metabolites in tissue, improved
              methods for drug extraction/ionization are required. Furthermore,
