               For Irganox 1010, the intensity of the deprotonated negative and
               the positive molecular ions increase as the square of the total
               ion yield. However, the intensity of intermediate fragments
               increase with a lower power, rising monotonically from unity at
               m/z ∼400 to 2 at the molecular ion. The constitution of the
               Irganox 1010 spectra for Ar+, Bi+, Bi$_{3}^{+}$ and Bi$_{5}^{+}$
               may be described by a basic spectrum such as that for Ar+ and two
               further ‘spectra’ which are product terms that multiply the
