              cells. Endothelial cytotoxicity was similarly augmented with mild
              hyperthermia applied prior to treatment with released CuDox. In
              summary, we find that the drug-metal complex formed in
              temperature-sensitive particles can be internalized by cancer and
              endothelial cells resulting in therapeutic efficacy that is
              similar to free doxorubicin, and this efficacy can be enhanced by
