              When compared to classical histology, the major benefit of this
              method is the ability to identify and localize many molecules in a
              single tissue sample. MALDI-MSI spatial resolution currently falls
              short of traditional microscopic methods as it is limited by
              instrumentation and sample preparation. Tissue preparation steps,
              such as matrix deposition, are critical when considering
              strategies to further enhance the spatial resolution. The
              mammalian retina was selected as the tissue of choice for method
              development; its stratified anatomy renders it an ideal tissue to
              test high-resolution MALDI-MSI as the different layers correspond
              to specific neuronal classes and cellular structures. We compared
