               surface was prepared for bone-targeted drug delivery. The
               distribution of ALN-PEG2k-ALN was tested by X-ray photoelectron
               spectroscopy. Isothermal titration calorimetry data indicated
               that similar to free ALN, both ALN-PEG2k-ALN and APA-CPNPs can
               bind to calcium ions. The bone-binding ability of APA-CPNPs was
               verified via ex vivo imaging of bone fragments. An in vitro
               release experiment demonstrated that APA-CPNPs can release drug
