  pages     = "33--50",
  abstract  = "Laser ablation–inductively coupled plasma-mass spectrometry
               (LA-ICP-MS) has been an invaluable tool for accurate and precise
               measurement of metals in geological and environmental samples.
               However, like many advanced analytical techniques its versatility
               has seen its translation into several other disciplines,
               including neuroimaging. In this chapter, we discuss the
               principles of LA-ICP-MS technology and how it is applied to
