               been applied to obtain detailed information on the chemical
               composition of biological materials, ranging from single
               microbial cells to tissues. Due to its compatibility with methods
               such as stable isotope labelling for the monitoring of cellular
               activities, vibrational spectroscopy also holds considerable
               power as a tool in microbial ecology. Chemical imaging of
