              accumulation are demonstrated on both model and real biological
              samples, indicating the high secondary ion efficiency afforded to
              the analyst by this primary ion when compared to other cluster ion
              beams used in imaging. The newly developed 40keV C60+ ion source
              allows the beam to be focused such that high resolution imaging is
              demonstrated on a tissue sample, and the greater yields allow the
              molecular signal from the drug raclopride to be imaged within
              tissue section following in vivo dosing. The localisation shown
