              as 40\%. On the other hand, steeper incidence angles led to a
              widening of the lateral dispersion of the secondary droplets and
              decreased analyte desorption. For all incidence angles, shorter
              probe distances were preferred since the resulting tighter
              dispersion of the secondary droplets produced higher ion
              transmission and therefore higher ambient MS signals. Tip height
