              works in concert with spike-timing-dependent plasticity (STDP) and
              what advantages their combination offers. Here we present a fairly
              large-scale functional model that uses leaky integrate-and-fire
              neurons, STDP, homeostasis, recurrent connections, and structural
              plasticity to learn the input encoding, the relation between
              inputs, and to infer missing inputs. Using this model, we compare
              the error and the amount of noise in the network's responses with
