              a combination of Catalyzed Amplification Reporter Deposition
              Fluorescence In-Situ Hybridization (CARD-FISH) and Nanoscale
              Secondary Ion Mass Spectrometry (NanoSIMS) to analyze community
              dynamics, single-cell activities and interactions among the two
              most abundant microbial community members (i.e, Gallionellaceae
              sp. and Bradyrhizobium spp.) under autotrophic and heterotrophic
              growth conditions. CARD-FISH cell counts showed the dominance of
