              associated with different areas of the brain were identified.
              Furthermore, glioblastoma tumor xenografts in a NOD/SCID mouse
              were imaged. Several glycans with differential expression in tumor
              versus normal brain tissues were identified. The MSI technique
              allows for imaging of N-glycans directly from FFPE sections. This
              method can potentially identify tissue-specific and/or
              disease-associated glycans coexpressed with other molecular
              signatures or within certain histological structures.",
  month    =  sep,
  year     =  2014
}

