              studied. TLE represents 40\% of the total epilepsy form of the
              disease and is difficult to treat. Despite a wealth of descriptive
              data obtained from the disease history of patients, the EEG
              recording, imaging techniques, and histological studies, the
              epileptogenic process remains poorly understood. However, it is
              unlikely that a single factor or a single mechanism can cause many
