  journal  = "Dev. Comp. Immunol.",
  volume   =  43,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "59--67",
  abstract = "The most abundant cell types in the hemolymph of Cupiennius salei
              are plasmatocytes (70-80\%) and granulocytes (20-30\%). Both cells
              differ in shape, cytochemical and transmission electron microscopy
              staining of their cytoplasma and granules. According to MALDI-IMS
