              specific compounds that have been determined to be biomarkers and
              therapeutic targets is relevant for the evaluation of the efficacy
              of targeted therapies. This article describes a new method called
              Spectro-ImmunoHistoChemistry (SIHC), which combines the use of
              specific antibodies against markers and mass spectrometric imaging
              in the MS/MS mode. SIHC is based on direct primary
              antibody-antigen recognition, trypsin digestion of the antibody
              overlaying the markers of interest in the tissue section, and
