              need for cancer biomarker tests and methods capable of
              discriminating between normal and malignant tissue. It is
              demonstrated that gold nanopartide enhanced target (AuNPET), a
              nano particle-based, surface-assisted laser desorption/ionization
              (SALDI)-type mass spectrometric method for analysis and imaging,
              can differentiate between normal and cancerous renal tissue.
              Diglyceride DG(18:1/20:0)-sodium adduct and protonated
              octadecanamide ions were found to have greatly elevated
