  volume   =  177,
  number   = "1-3",
  pages    = "67--69",
  abstract = "Understanding the molecular basis of schizophrenia is essential
              for disease management, and several molecular biology tools have
              been employed for this purpose. Mass spectrometry, which is used
              mostly in proteomic and metabolomic studies, is one such tool.
              Here, we present the first psychiatric study to use mass
              spectrometry imaging (MSI) with desorption electrospray ionization
              (DESI). Preparation of samples for use with DESI-MSI is remarkably
              simple and quick and preserves the spatial distribution of
