              applied to obtain 2D molecular images of the major dyes used for
              staining, that is, 1-methylaminoanthraquinone (MAAQ), rhodamine B
              (RB) and rhodamine 6G (R6G). MAAQ could not be detected because of
              its inefficient desorption by DESI from the banknote cellulose
              surface. By contrast, ATD staining on banknotes is perceptible by
              the human naked eye only at concentrations higher than 0.2 mu g
