  journal  = "Methods",
  volume   =  104,
  pages    = "93--100",
  abstract = "Mass spectrometry imaging (MSI) is a powerful tool for the study
              of intact tissue sections. The use of matrix-assisted laser
              desorption/ionisation (MALDI) MSI for the study of the
              distribution and effect of emollient treatment on sections of
              reconstructed living skin equivalents during their development and
              maturation is described. Living skin equivalent (LSE) samples were
              obtained at 14 days development, re-suspended in maintenance
              medium and incubated for 24 h after delivery. The medium was
