              distributions. The implications of these results for laser
              ablation sampling and mass spectrometry imaging under ambient
              conditions are discussed.",
  year     =  2016
}

@ARTICLE{Castellanos2016-jh,
  title    = "Characterization of firearm discharge residues recovered from skin
              swabs using sub-micrometric mass spectrometry imaging",
  author   = "Castellanos, Anthony and Bell, Suzanne and Fernandez-Lima,
              Francisco",
  journal  = "Anal. Methods",
  volume   =  8,
  number   =  21,
  pages    = "4300--4305",
  abstract = "In the present work, we show the advantages of high spatial
              resolution interrogation of firearm discharge residues from skin
              swabs using ion bombardment coupled to mass spectrometry. In
              particular, the collection of secondary ion and electron maps
              permitted the chemical (organic and inorganic) and morphological
              characterization of particulates and organic compounds
