  author   = "Janfelt, Christian",
  editor   = "He, L",
  journal  = "MASS SPECTROMETRY IMAGING OF SMALL MOLECULES",
  volume   =  1203,
  pages    = "91--97",
  abstract = "Indirect desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
              (DESI-MS) imaging is a method for imaging distributions of
              metabolites in plant materials, in particular leaves and petals.
              The challenge in direct imaging of such plant materials with
              DESI-MS is particularly the protective layer of cuticular wax
              present in leaves and petals. The cuticle protects the plant from
              drying out, but also makes it difficult for the DESI sprayer to
              reach the analytes of interest inside the plant material. A
              solution to this problem is to imprint the plant material onto a
              surface, thus releasing the analytes of interest from parts of
