              tissue insulates primordia from entrance by intrinsic ice. Water
              repellent and densely packed bud scales prevent extrinsic ice
              penetration. At -18 degrees C, break-down of supercooling was
              triggered by intrinsic ice nucleators whereas the ice barrier
              remained active. Temperature-dependent freeze dehydration
              (-0.1MPaK(-1)) caused accumulation of extraorgan ice masses that
