              ResultsNanoparticle-enhanced mass spectrometry imaging made it
              possible to study the distribution of selected compounds in the
              European yew tissue, including taxanes - terpene alkaloids
              characteristic for the Taxus genus. Results prove that aspartate,
              taxinine M, baccatin IV and taxine B are located mainly in the
