  volume   =  28,
  number   =  12,
  pages    = "2635--2645",
  abstract = "Mass spectrometry imaging datasets are mostly analyzed in terms of
              average intensity in regions of interest. However, biological
              tissues have different morphologies with several sizes, shapes,
              and structures. The important biological information, contained in
              this highly heterogeneous cellular organization, could be hidden
              by analyzing the average intensities. Finding an analytical
