              by matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization-mass spectrometry
              imaging (MALDI-MSI). Formal in-inflation enables sample
              preparation to parallel standard clinical and surgical procedures,
              in addition to greatly reducing the complexity of analysis, by
              decreasing the number of analytes in the MALDI plume and reducing
              adduct formation in the resulting mass spectra. The reduced
              complexity increased sensitivity and enabled high-resolution
              imaging acquisitions without any loss in analyte detection at 10
              and 20 mu m scans. We present a detailed study of over 100 lipid
              ions detected in positive and negative ion modes covering the
              conducting and respiratory airways and parts of the peripheral
              nervous tissue running through the lungs. By defining the
