               three different bin sizes of 0.25, 0.5 and 1.0 were chosen.
               Afterwards, three-way MSI data arrays (two spatial and one m/z
               dimensions) for seven standards and four unknown samples were
               column-wise augmented with m/z values as common mode. Then, these
               data sets were analyzed using multivariate curve
               resolution-alternating least squares (MCR-ALS) using proper
               constraints. The resolved mass spectra were used for
               identification of chlordecone in the presence of complex
               background and interferences. Additionally, the augmented spatial
