              decision tree classifier, which classifies about 72\% of patients
              correctly. Almost all the predictive power comes from a single
              peak (m/z 718.4). The sensitivity of our classification approach,
              which can be generically used to search for biomarkers, is
              investigated using artificially modified data.",
