  journal  = "bioRxiv",
  pages    =  518977,
  abstract = "Motivation: Imaging mass spectrometry (imaging MS) is a powerful
              technology for revealing localizations of hundreds of molecules in
              tissue sections. However, imaging MS data is polluted with
              off-sample ions caused by caused by sample preparation,
              particularly by the MALDI matrix application. The presence of the
              off-sample ion images confounds and hinders metabolite
              identification and downstream analysis. Results: We created a
              high-quality gold standard of 23238 manually tagged ion images
