               tools to assist the exploration of the remaining volume of
               unknown data in terms of demonstrating similarity or discordance
               in tissue compartment distribution patterns. Here we present a
               novel, interactive approach to extract information from MSI data
               that relies on precalculated data structures to perform queries
               of large data sets with a typical laptop. We have devised methods
               to query the full volume to find new m/z values of potential
               interest based on similarity to biological structures or to the
               spatial distribution of known ions. We describe these query
               methods in detail and provide examples demonstrating the power of
               the methods to ``discover'' m/z values of ions that have such
