              isocitrate dehydrogenase (IDH)-dependent reductive carboxylation,
              producing the reductive power necessary to quench reactive oxygen
              species (ROS) originated during the switch from two-dimensional
              (2D) to three-dimensional (3D) growth (a necessary hallmark of
