              and Harrison, Robert A and Blanksby, Stephen J and Undheim, Eivind
              Andreas Baste",
  journal  = "Angew. Chem. Int. Ed Engl.",
  abstract = "Enzymes are central components of most physiological processes,
              and are consequently implicated in various pathologies.
              High-resolution maps of enzyme activity within tissues therefore
              represent powerful tools for elucidating enzymatic functions in
              health and disease. Here, we present a novel mass spectrometry
              imaging (MSI) method for assaying the spatial distribution of
              enzymatic activity directly from tissue. MSI analysis of tissue
              sections exposed to phospholipid substrates produced
