              constructed from a large BC cohort (n = 803). Patients were
              stratified based on SLC protein expression into accredited
              clusters and correlated with immune cell infiltrates and patient
              outcome. The effect of transient siRNA knockdown of SLC7A5 and
              SLC1A5 on PDL1 expression was evaluated in MDA-MB-231 cells.
              RESULTS: High SLCs were significantly associated with PDL1 and PD1
              +, FOXP3 +, CD68 + and CD20 + cells (p < 0.001). Triple negative
              (TN), HER2 + and luminal B tumours showed variable associations
              between SLCs and immune cell types (p ≤ 0.04). The expression of
              SLCs and PDL1, PD1 +, FOXP3 + and CD68 + cells was associated with
              poor patient outcome (p < 0.001). Knockdown of SLC7A5
              significantly reduced PDL1 expression. CONCLUSION: This study
