               over-the-counter and prescription tablet formations was
               demonstrated for amphetamine (methylphenidate), antidepressant
               (venlafaxine), barbiturate (Barbituric acid), depressant
               (alprazolam), narcotic (3-methylmorphine) and sympatholytic
               (propranolol) drugs. Active ingredients from soft and liquid
               formulations, such as Icy Hot cream (methyl salicylate) and
               Nyquil cold medicine (acetaminophen, dextromethorphan,
               doxylamine) were also detected. Increased sensitivity for
               selective drug responses was demonstrated through the formation
               of sodiated adduct ions by introducing small quantities of NaCl
               into the DESI solvent. Of the drugs and pharmaceuticals tested in
