               accurate model for product authentication. A Support Vector
               Machine (SVM) model was finally chosen for the swNIR, providing
               100\% of correct identification in calibration and 96.0\% in
               validation, and a Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA) model was
               chosen for the cNIR delivering 99.9\% of correct identification
               in calibration and 91.1\% in validation. Challenging samples
               (counterfeits and generics) could be 100\% identified by the
