              standard treatments for GBM, the median survival is still about
              one year. Analysis of brain tissues from GBM patients shows that
              lipid droplets are highly enriched in tumor tissues while
              undetectable in normal brain tissues, yet the identity and
              functions of lipid species in GBM are not well understood. The
              aims of the present work are to determine how GBM utilizes fatty
              acids, and assess their roles in GBM proliferation. Treatment of
              U138 GBM cells with a monounsaturated fatty acid, oleic acid,
              induces accumulation of perilipin 2-coated lipid droplets
