              mass spectrometry to image host–microbe symbioses and their
              metabolic interactions. The metaFISH pipeline aligns and
              integrates metabolite and fluorescent images at the micrometre
              scale to provide a spatial assignment of host and symbiont
              metabolites on the same tissue section. To illustrate the
              advantages of metaFISH, we mapped the spatial metabolome of a
              deep-sea mussel and its intracellular symbiotic bacteria at the
