  pages    = "2321--2333",
  abstract = "Endothelial metabolism is a key regulator of angiogenesis.
              Glutamine metabolism in endothelial cells (ECs) has been poorly
              studied. We used genetic modifications and 13C tracing approaches
              to define glutamine metabolism in these cells. Glutamine supplies
              the majority of carbons in the tricyclic acid (TCA) cycle of ECs
