  pages     = "1--7",
  abstract  = "The use of mass spectrometry imaging (MSI) techniques has become
               a powerful tool in the fields of biology, pharmacology and
               healthcare. Next generation experimental techniques are able to
               generate 100s of gigabytes of data from a single image
               acquisition and thus require advanced algorithms in order to
               analyse these data. At present, analytical work-flows begin with
