  journal  = "BMC Bioinformatics",
  volume   =  21,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  129,
  abstract = "BACKGROUND: Imaging mass spectrometry (imaging MS) is an enabling
              technology for spatial metabolomics of tissue sections with
              rapidly growing areas of applications in biology and medicine.
              However, imaging MS data is polluted with off-sample ions caused
              by sample preparation, particularly by the MALDI (matrix-assisted
