  journal  = "Sci. Rep.",
  volume   =  9,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  7247,
  abstract = "Chemical imaging by mass spectrometry (MS) has been largely used
              to study diseases in animals and humans, especially cancer;
              however, this technology has been minimally explored to study the
              complex chemical changes associated with fetal development. In
              this work, we report the histologically-compatible chemical
              imaging of small molecules by desorption electrospray ionization
