  volume   =  9,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  3192,
  abstract = "Mass spectrometry imaging (MSI) provides label-free, non-targeted
              molecular and spatial information of the biomolecules within
              tissue. Lipids play important roles in lung biology, e.g. as
              surfactant, preventing alveolar collapse during normal and forced
              respiration. Lipidomic characterization of late fetal mouse lungs
