               more importantly the spatial information of these molecules in
               cartilage is still poorly understood. Matrix-assisted laser
               desorption/ionization (MALDI) mass spectrometry imaging (MSI) has
               been previously used for the investigation of the bimolecular
               distribution of proteins and lipids through the in situ analysis
               of cartilage tissue sections. MALDI-MSI as a tool to detect
               metabolites remains challenging, as these species have low
               abundance and degrade rapidly. In this work, we present a
