              nanoscale and subcellular compartments. We adapt expansion
              microscopy, which physically expands biological specimens, for
              long-read untargeted and targeted in situ RNA sequencing. We
              applied untargeted expansion sequencing (ExSeq) to mouse brain,
              yielding readout of thousands of genes, including splice variants
              and novel transcripts. Targeted ExSeq yielded nanoscale-resolution
              maps of RNAs throughout dendrites and spines in neurons of the
              mouse hippocampus, revealing patterns across multiple cell types;
