              discovered that modulation of the Hippo pathway acts as a
              ``modifier'' for neurofibroma tumorigenesis. This mouse model
              opens the doors for deciphering the evolution of cNF to identify
              effective therapies, where none exist today. SIGNIFICANCE: This
              study provides insights into the developmental origin of cNF, the
              most common tumor in NF1, and generates the first mouse model that
              faithfully recapitulates both human cutaneous and plexiform
