               and ultimate cellular fate of the NPs is necessary to satisfy
               safety concerns, which is difficult because of the nanoscale size
               of these carriers. In this work, we show how small chemical
               labels can be appended to poly(lactic acid-co-glycolic acid)
               (PLGA) to synthesize NPs that can then be imaged by stimulated
               Raman scattering microscopy, a vibrational imaging technique that
               can elucidate bond-specific information in biological
               environments, such as the identification of alkyne signatures in
