  pages    = "985--995",
  abstract = "To chart cell composition and cell state changes that occur during
              the transformation of healthy colon to precancerous adenomas to
              colorectal cancer (CRC), we generated single-cell chromatin
              accessibility profiles and single-cell transcriptomes from 1,000
              to 10,000 cells per sample for 48 polyps, 27 normal tissues and 6
              CRCs collected from patients with or without germline APC
              mutations. A large fraction of polyp and CRC cells exhibit a
              stem-like phenotype, and we define a continuum of epigenetic and
              transcriptional changes occurring in these stem-like cells as they
