  volume   =  17,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "169--177",
  abstract = "OBJECTIVE: Many healthcare organizations follow data protection
              policies that specify which patient identifiers must be suppressed
              to share ``de-identified'' records. Such policies, however, are
              often applied without knowledge of the risk of
              ``re-identification''. The goals of this work are: (1) to estimate
              re-identification risk for data sharing policies of the Health
