  volume    =  25,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "307--314",
  abstract  = "Digital slide images produced from routine diagnostic
               histopathological preparations suffer from variation arising at
               every step of the processing pipeline. Typically, pathologists
               compensate for such variation using expert knowledge and
               experience, which is difficult to replicate in automated
               solutions. The extent to which inconsistencies affect image
               analysis is explored in this work, examining in detail, the
