              Neumann, Steffen and Nielsen, Jens and Perez de Souza, Leonardo
              and Saito, Kazuki and Sauer, Uwe and Schroeder, Frank C and
              Schuster, Stefan and Siuzdak, Gary and Skirycz, Aleksandra and
              Sumner, Lloyd W and Snyder, Michael P and Tang, Huiru and Tohge,
              Takayuki and Wang, Yulan and Wen, Weiwei and Wu, Si and Xu,
              Guowang and Zamboni, Nicola and Fernie, Alisdair R",
  journal  = "Nat. Methods",
  volume   =  18,
  number   =  7,
  pages    = "747--756",
  abstract = "Mass spectrometry-based metabolomics approaches can enable
              detection and quantification of many thousands of metabolite
              features simultaneously. However, compound identification and
              reliable quantification are greatly complicated owing to the
              chemical complexity and dynamic range of the metabolome.
              Simultaneous quantification of many metabolites within complex
              mixtures can additionally be complicated by ion suppression,
              fragmentation and the presence of isomers. Here we present
