              and Liu, X Shirley and White, Kevin P and Gerstein, Mark",
  journal  = "Nat. Commun.",
  volume   =  11,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  3696,
  abstract = "ENCODE comprises thousands of functional genomics datasets, and
              the encyclopedia covers hundreds of cell types, providing a
              universal annotation for genome interpretation. However, for
              particular applications, it may be advantageous to use a
              customized annotation. Here, we develop such a custom annotation
              by leveraging advanced assays, such as eCLIP, Hi-C, and
              whole-genome STARR-seq on a number of data-rich ENCODE cell types.
              A key aspect of this annotation is comprehensive and
              experimentally derived networks of both transcription factors and
              RNA-binding proteins (TFs and RBPs). Cancer, a disease of
