              consider some ethical problems it might be thought to pose. These
              arise from (1) the tension between artificial intelligence (AI)
              research-with its hunger for more and more data-and the default
              preference in data ethics and data protection law for the
              minimisation of personal data collection and processing; (2) the
              fact that computational pathology lends itself to kinds of data
