               find that membrane RSK1 mediates negative feedback on WT RAS
               signaling and impedes the proliferation of pancreatic cancer
               cells upon the ablation of mutant KRAS. Our findings link NF1 to
               the membrane-localized functions of RSK1 and highlight a role for
               WT RAS signaling in promoting adaptive resistance to mutant
               KRAS-specific inhibitors in PDAC.",
  month     =  may,
  year      =  2021,
  keywords  = "BioID; KRAS; NF1; PDAC; RSK",
