  abstract = "MOTIVATION: Mass spectrometry imaging (MSI) characterizes the
              spatial distribution of ions in complex biological samples such as
              tissues. Since many tissues have complex morphology, treatments
              and conditions often affect the spatial distribution of the ions
              in morphology-specific ways. Evaluating the selectivity and the
              specificity of ion localization and regulation across morphology
              types is biologically important. However, MSI lacks algorithms for
              segmenting images at both single-ion and spatial resolution.
