  volume    =  6,
  number    =  1,
  pages     =  37648,
  abstract  = "Liquid extraction surface analysis mass spectrometry imaging
               (LESA-MSI) has been shown to be an effective tissue profiling and
               imaging technique, producing robust and reliable qualitative
               distribution images of an analyte or analytes in tissue sections.
               Here, we expand the use of LESA-MSI beyond qualitative analysis
               to a quantitative analytical technique by employing a mimetic
               tissue model previously shown to be applicable for MALDI-MSI
               quantitation. Liver homogenate was used to generate a viable and
               molecularly relevant control matrix for spiked drug standards
               which can be frozen, sectioned and subsequently analyzed for the
