              to the brittle hydrophobic cuticle surrounding the body and
              heterogeneous tissue types beneath the cuticle. However, the
              introduction of a novel sucrose infiltration step and gelatin as
              an embedding media greatly improved the quality of tissue
              sections. We generated MS image profiles of six major lipid
              classes: phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine,
              phosphatidylglycerol, phosphatidylinositol, phosphatidylserine,
              and triacylglycerides. In addition, signals corresponding to two
