               round robin (interlaboratory comparison) was organized between
               four laboratories on identical samples using AES, XPS and SIMS.
               The sample consisted of an Ni/Cr multilayer with a total of 16
               alternating Ni and Cr layers with a singly layer thickness of 30
               nm. Sputter profiling was performed with a rastered beam of 3 keV
               Ar+ ions at an incidence angle of 45° to the surface normal, with
               and without sample rotation. Test runs were additionally
               performed with BCR standard samples of 30 nm thick Ta2O5 layers
               on Ta. For sample rotation, depth profiles of the Ni/Cr
               multilayer by AES and SIMS show a marked improvement in depth
