  pages     = "1582--1596",
  abstract  = "The extracellular haemoglobin of the marine polychaete, Arenicola
               marina, is a hexagonal bilayer haemoglobin of approximately 3600
               kDa, formed by the covalent and noncovalent association of many
               copies of both globin subunits (monomer and trimer) and nonglobin
