              individually estimated from a suitably designed set of
              experiments. The values of the Thiele modulus from the kinetic
              parameters so calculated have been found to be in the range 1.67
              to 9.8 for the two enzymes studied, implying that diffusional
              effects cannot be ignored. The effect of such diffusional
              limitations on the overall rates and hence on the utilisation of
              the intrinsic kinetic ability of the enzyme has been demonstrated.
