  pages    = "63--88",
  abstract = "Modified polysiloxane membranes containing different
              organofunctional side chains were produced and tested for the
              recovery of various organic contaminants from aqueous streams,
              using the process of pervaporation. Four separate organic
              components, phenol, chloroform, pyridine and methylisobutylketone
              (MIBK), each representative of an industrially significant family
