              cells on substrates coated with different densities of ECM,
              suggested that cell shape may play an important role in control of
              apoptosis as well as growth. Data are presented which show how
              micropatterned substrates were used to definitively test this
              hypothesis. Progressively restricting bovine and human endothelial
              cell extension by culturing cells on smaller and smaller
              micropatterned adhesive islands regulated a transition from growth
              to apoptosis on a single continuum of cell spreading, thus
