              resulting hydrogel in the presence of glucose led to changes in
              the diffusion rate observed for a range of proteins. Gels of
              specified thickness were cast around to nylon gauze support (pore
              size, 0.1 mm) to improve mechanical strength. Diffusion of
              proteins through the gel membrane was determined using a
              twin-chamber diffusion cell with the concentrations being
              continuously monitored using a UV-spectrophotometer. Changes in
