  number   =  19,
  pages    = "4427--4436",
  abstract = "The assembly of fibronectin into a fibrillar matrix is a regulated
              step-wise process that involves binding to integrin receptors and
              interactions between fibronectin molecules. This process has been
              studied extensively using cells in two-dimensional (2D) monolayer
              culture. In most situations in vivo, however, matrix assembly
              occurs within existing three-dimensional (3D) extracellular matrix
              networks. In an attempt to mimic this environment, we analyzed
              matrix assembly by fibroblasts cultured on a pre-assembled 3D
              fibronectin matrix and found significant stimulation of
              fibronectin fibril assembly compared to cells in 2D culture. Lower
