  pages    = "360--371",
  abstract = "Cannabinoids have long been proposed to affect the immune system,
              especially as one of the cannabinoid receptors, the cannabinoid
              receptor-2 (CB(2)R) has been found almost exclusively on immune
              cells. Here, using human in vitro activated peripheral
              blood-derived T lymphocytes we investigated the long-term changes
              in cannabinoid receptor protein expression following cellular
              activation and the effects of cannabinoids on migration. We report
