               cartilage formed by primary chondrocytes exhibited only small
               increases in GAG content. However, all passaged chondrocytes on
               day 28 elaborated a cartilage matrix with compressive properties
               and GAG content in the range of native, adult, canine cartilage
               values. A preliminary biocompatibility study utilizing chondral
               and osteochondral constructs showed no gross or histological
               signs of rejection, with all implanted constructs showing
