  journal   = "Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U. S. A.",
  publisher = "National Acad Sciences",
  abstract  = "Although adipose tissue is an expandable and readily attainable
               source of proliferating, multipotent stem cells, its potential
               for use in regenerative medicine has not been extensively
               explored. Here we report that adult human and mouse
               adipose-derived stem cells can be reprogrammed to induced
               pluripotent stem (iPS) cells with substantially higher
               efficiencies than those reported for human and mouse fibroblasts.
