              Buddy D",
  journal  = "Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U. S. A.",
  volume   =  107,
  number   =  34,
  pages    = "15211--15216",
  abstract = "We demonstrate here a cardiac tissue-engineering strategy
              addressing multicellular organization, integration into host
              myocardium, and directional cues to reconstruct the functional
              architecture of heart muscle. Microtemplating is used to shape
              poly(2-hydroxyethyl methacrylate-co-methacrylic acid) hydrogel
              into a tissue-engineering scaffold with architectures driving
              heart tissue integration. The construct contains parallel channels
