              (TIC) has not been identified. In this study, the relevance of the
              CSC model in NB was investigated by taking advantage of typical
              functional stem cell characteristics. A predictive association was
              established between self-renewal, as assessed by serial sphere
              formation, and clinical aggressiveness in primary tumors.
              Moreover, cell subsets gradually selected during serial sphere
              culture harbored increased in vivo tumorigenicity, only
              highlighted in an orthotopic microenvironment. A microarray time
              course analysis of serial spheres passages from metastatic cells
              allowed us to specifically ``profile'' the NB stem cell-like
              phenotype and to identify CD133, ABC transporter, and WNT and
