  number    =  14,
  pages     = "3575--3583",
  abstract  = "One of the obstacles to the potential clinical utility of
               bioengineered skeletal muscle is its limited force generation
               capacity. Since engineered muscle, unlike most native muscle
               tissue, is composed of relatively short myofibers, we
               hypothesized that, its force production and transmission would be
