  volume    =  32,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "9--9",
  abstract  = "Biomaterials are increasingly being used to engineer the
               biochemical and biophysical properties of the extracellular stem
               cell microenvironment in order to tailor niche characteristics
               and direct cell phenotype. To date, stem cell-biomaterial
               interactions have largely been studied by introducing stem cells
               into artificial environments, such as 2D cell culture on
