  volume    =  43,
  number    = "1-2",
  pages     = "555--558",
  abstract  = "Micropatterning is used widely in biosensor development, tissue
               engineering and basic biology. Creation of biological
               micropatterns typically involves multiple sequential steps that
               may lead to cross-contamination and may contribute to sub-optimal
               performance of the surface. Therefore, there is a need to develop
