  number   =  9,
  pages    = "3324--3327",
  abstract = "Cancer treatment with the drug cisplatin is often thwarted by the
              emergence of drug-resistant cells. To study this phenomenon, we
              identified two independent cellular factors that recognize
              cisplatin-damaged DNA. One of the two factors, designated XPE
              binding factor, is deficient in complementation group E of
