  volume   =  117,
  number   =  3,
  pages    = "358--363",
  abstract = "The arterial media is modeled as a periodic array of cylindrical
              smooth muscle cells residing in a matrix comprised of proteoglycan
              and collagen fibers. Using Brinkman's model to describe transmural
              flow through such a fibrous media, we calculate the effective
              hydraulic permeability of the media and the wall shear stress on
