  number    =  2,
  pages     = "460--465",
  abstract  = "Bone sialoprotein (BSP) and osteopontin (OPN) are two members of
               the SIBLING (Small Integrin-Binding LIgand, N-linked
               Glycoprotein) family of genetically related proteins that are
               clustered on human chromosome 4. We present evidence that this
               entire family is the result of duplication and subsequent
               divergent evolution of a single ancient gene. The solution
               structures of these two post-translationally modified recombinant
