  journal  = "Eur. Cell. Mater.",
  volume   =  4,
  pages    = "1--17",
  abstract = "Implant loosening in bone fixation is an unresolved complication
              associated with internal fixation. It is generally accepted that
              this problem can be overcome by modifying the implant/bone
              interface for improved osseointegration. This is achieved, in
              part, by hydroxyapatite (HA) or tricalcium phosphate coatings.
              Unfortunately, the benefits of these coatings are constrained by
