              Anodic Plasma-chemical treatment (APC) has been developed to
              incorporate electrolytes and produce coatings with various
              microtopographies and strong adhesion to implants. In this in
              vitro study fibroblast and osteoblast morphologies and adhesion to
              various substrates were evaluated using qualitative and
              quantitative methods. The substrates were Thermanox plastic and
              commercially pure titanium. The latter were surface-treated using
              several different methods: conventional anodisation, plasma
              spraying of HA and anodic plasma-chemical (APC) treatment in an
              electrolyte solution containing either calcium and phosphate
              (APC-CaP) or phosphoric acid (APC-P). Both osteoblasts and
