  volume    =  13,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "407--428",
  abstract  = "Characterization of biomaterial surfaces requires analytical
               techniques that are capable of detecting a wide concentration
               range of adsorbed protein. This range includes detection of low
               amounts of adsorbed protein (<10 ng/cm2) that may be present on
               non-fouling biomaterials. X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS)
