  volume    =  22,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "241--249",
  abstract  = "Skeletal homeostasis is partly regulated by the mechanical
               environment and specific signals generated by a cell's adhesion
               to the matrix. Previous studies demonstrated that osteopontin
               (OPN) expression is stimulated in response to both cellular
               adhesion and mechanical stimulation. The present studies examine
               if specific integrin ligands mediate osteoblast selective
