  volume   =  282,
  number   =  21,
  pages    = "15872--15883",
  abstract = "Inorganic pyrophosphate (PP(i)) produced by cells inhibits
              mineralization by binding to crystals. Its ubiquitous presence is
              thought to prevent ``soft'' tissues from mineralizing, whereas its
              degradation to P(i) in bones and teeth by tissue-nonspecific
