              indicated that the outer surface of the coatings (without a PLGA
              capcoat) were drug-rich prior to elution. TOF-SIMS depth profiling
              using SF5+ polyatomic primary ions revealed a drug-enriched region
              at the near surface of the non-capcoated coatings ranging in
              thickness from 5 to 115 nm. The chemical morphology of the
              rapamycin/PLGA coatings on stents was determined using scanning
              confocal Raman microscopy, from the surface through the bulk of
              the coatings. Images of the coatings on stents showed a
