  volume    =  28,
  number    =  14,
  pages     = "2281--2293",
  abstract  = "Microfabricated tapered pits in vivo can stimulate connective
               tissue and bone attachment to percutaneous devices, secondarily
               preventing epithelial migration, and promoting long-term implant
               survival. Epithelial cells, which form a seal with a dental
               implant, acting as a barrier, and osteoblasts, which form bone,
