  number    =  12,
  pages     = "4465--4474",
  abstract  = "The complex pathogenesis of mineralization defects seen in
               inherited and/or acquired hypophosphatemic disorders suggests
               that local inorganic phosphate (P(i)) regulation by osteoblasts
               may be a rate-limiting step in physiological bone mineralization.
               To test whether an osteoblast autonomous phosphate regulatory
