  volume   =  41,
  number   =  6,
  pages    = "1374--1378",
  abstract = "In vitro bone tissue growth inside porous scaffolds can be
              enhanced by macroscopic cyclic compression of the construct, but
              the heterogeneous strain generated inside the construct must be
              investigated to determine appropriate levels of compression. For
              this purpose a linear micro-finite element (muFE) technique based
              on micro-computed tomography (muCT) was verified for the
