              neurosensory hearing loss are, at present, the only therapy for
              these people. In contrast to this therapy, replacement of hair
              cells via stem cell therapies holds the promise for a cure. We
              review here current insights into embryonic, adult, and inducible
              stem cells that might provide cells for seeding the cochlea with
              the hope of new hair cell formation. We propose a two-step
              approach using a first set of transcription factors to enhance the
              generation of inducible pluripotent stem (iPS) cells and a second
