              fibrocartilage or mixed (hyaline-fibrocartilage) tissue, while
              tissues taken from asymptomatic patients were hyaline cartilage in
              83\% of biopsies. In a small group of asymptomatic patients (n =
              3), second-look and third-look biopsies taken 18 months after
              surgery confirmed maturation of the newly formed tissue over time.
              Cartilage maturation occurred from the inner regions of the graft,
              in contact with subchondral bone, towards the periphery of the
              implant. CONCLUSIONS: The study indicates that, in asymptomatic
              patients after chondrocyte implantation, regenerated tissue
