              decellularized scaffolds. This study was performed to determine
              the glycosaminoglycans content, distribution, and disaccharides
              composition in porcine aortic and pulmonary valves and in
              pericardium before and after a detergent-based decellularization
              procedure. The fine structural characteristics of
              galactosaminoglycans chondroitin sulfate and dermatan sulfate were
              examined by FACE. Furthermore, the mechanical properties of
              decellularized pericardium and its propensity to be repopulated by
