              elucidate wide-ranging cell and cytoskeletal responses to E in
              both 2D and 3D matrix geometries. Cross-linked hyaluronic acid
              (HA) based matrices as well as standard polyacrylamide (PA)
              hydrogels show that, within hours of initial plating, the
              adhesion, asymmetric shape, and cytoskeletal order within
              mesenchymal stem cells generally depend on E nonmonotonically over
              a broad range of physiologically relevant E. In particular, with
              overlays of a second matrix the stiffer of the upper or lower
              matrix dominates key cell responses to 3D: the cell invariably
