               In vivo xenografting is commonly used to study cellular
               interactions not mimicked or quantified in conventional 2D
               culture systems. To interrogate the effects of tumor stroma
               (cancer-associated fibroblasts or CAFs) on epithelia, we created
               a bioengineered microenvironment using human prostatic tissues.
