  journal   = "Nat. Mater.",
  publisher = "Nature Publishing Group",
  abstract  = "Although cell-matrix adhesive interactions are known to regulate
               stem cell differentiation, the underlying mechanisms, in
               particular for direct three-dimensional encapsulation within
               hydrogels, are poorly understood. Here, we demonstrate that in
               covalently crosslinked hyaluronic acid (HA) hydrogels, the
               differentiation of human mesenchymal stem cells (hMSCs) is
               directed by the generation of degradation-mediated cellular
               traction, independently of cell morphology or matrix mechanics.
