                   combination of the above three parameters, the ultimate depth
                   resolution is predicted to be about 0.7-1.0 nm. Up to now,
                   values of 1.4-1.6 nm have been reported, and the use of low
                   energy molecular ions, e.g. by using sulfur hexafluoride as
                   sputtering gas, has recently pushed the mixing length down to
                   0.4-0.6 nm. However, particularly in depth profiling of
                   multilayers, it can be shown that minimizing the rouhgness
