  number    =  15,
  pages     = "3792--3802",
  abstract  = "The host response to biomaterials has been studied for decades.
               Largely, the interaction of host immune cells, macrophages in
               particular, with implanted materials has been considered to be a
               precursor to granulation tissue formation, the classic foreign
               body reaction, and eventual encapsulation with associated
               negative impacts upon device functionality. However, more
               recently, it has been shown that macrophages, depending upon
               context dependent polarization profiles, are capable of affecting
               both detrimental and beneficial outcomes in a number of disease
